<title>USA: PSE&amp;G 1,031 MW N.J. nuke in startup mode.</title>
<headline>PSE&amp;G 1,031 MW N.J. nuke in startup mode.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public Service Enterprise Group Inc said Thursday its 1,031 megawatt Hope Creek nuclear power plant was in startup mode and likely to be contributing electricity to the grid later in the day.</p>
<p>&quot;It will probably synchronize to the grid sometime this evening,&quot; spokeswoman Tricia DuBois said Thursday.</p>
<p>The Salem, N.J., plant was shut down Nov 2 for repairs to valves in the reactor's recirculating system.</p>
<p>Public Service Enterprise is the operator and majority owner of the Hope Creek plant.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
